; Frac of a Quick assigned to a Quick in AB3 mode (change
; compiler-intrinsics, spec compiler/intrinsics): the fraction with the
; sign of the value.  AB3 mode's vallib (AmiBlitz3's) takes a Float for
; Frac, which is not the form of the intrinsic: the call stays ("calls 3":
; qutofl, Frac, fltoqu), as in AmiBlitz3
Function.l jsrs{a.l,b.l}
  n.l = 0
  While a < b
    If Peek.w(a) = $4EB9
      n = n + 1 : a = a + 4
    EndIf
    a = a + 2
  Wend
  Function Return n
End Function
q1.q = 0 : q2.q = 0
q1 = 1.25 : q2 = Frac(q1) : NPrint q2
q1 = -1.25 : q2 = Frac(q1) : NPrint q2
q1 = 0.5 : q2 = Frac(q1) : NPrint q2
q1 = -3 : q2 = Frac(q1) : NPrint q2
q1 = 300.75 : q2 = Frac(q1) : NPrint q2
q1 = -1.25
.a1
q2 = Frac(q1)
.a2
NPrint q2, " calls ", jsrs{?a1, ?a2}
End
